#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:262
msgid "Your host adds its own caching instructions to the blyg"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: URL, 2: the Cache-Control header as received, 3: mount path, 4: a length of time, such as "5 mins"
#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:264
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s arrives with caching instructions that are not the plugin's (%2$s). The plugin puts its own lifetime (%4$s) first, and a cache follows the first it reads; here a longer one, added by the web server or by something else in front of WordPress, comes first. An item you withdraw, or a post you edit, could keep being served in its old form. If a plugin or theme on this site filters soapbox_blyg_cache_control, its value must keep s-maxage. Otherwise this comes from the server's own configuration, so excluding the path from a page cache does not remove it: ask your host to stop adding a Cache-Control header for %3$s and for /wp-json/soapbox-blyg/."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:293
msgid "A cache in front of this site is serving an old copy of the blyg"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: URL, 2: mount path
#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:295
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s was answered with a copy that is not the document as it is now. Something in front of WordPress (a CDN, Varnish, or your host's own cache) kept an earlier one and has not been told it changed. An item you withdraw, or a post you edit, keeps being served in its old form from there. Purge that cache now. So that it does not happen again, exclude the path %2$s, and the REST namespace /wp-json/soapbox-blyg/, from it, or connect it to the soapbox_blyg_purge_urls action. The plugin's readme lists the cache plugins it purges by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:305
msgid "A cache in front of this site is holding the blyg"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: URL, 2: mount path, 3: a length of time, such as "5 mins"
#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:307
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s is being served from a shared cache (a CDN, Varnish, or your host's own cache) for longer than the cache lifetime in the plugin's settings (%3$s). An item you withdraw, or a post you edit, would keep being served in its old form until that cache expires. Exclude the path %2$s, and the REST namespace /wp-json/soapbox-blyg/, from that cache. The plugin's readme has instructions for Varnish, Cloudflare and nginx."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:318
msgid "The blyg's caching could not be checked from the server"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: a number of seconds
#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:320
#, php-format
msgid "This site could not request its own blyg, so it cannot tell whether a cache in front of it is holding the documents. To check by hand, request the manifest twice, a few seconds apart, and look at the response headers: the first s-maxage in Cache-Control should be %1$d, and Age should never be more than %1$d."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:327
msgid "The copies of the blyg being served are current"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: a length of time, such as "5 mins"
#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:329
#, php-format
msgid "A cache in front of this site keeps the blyg's documents for longer than the cache lifetime in the plugin's settings (%s), and the copies it is serving are the documents as they are now. That is safe for as long as the cache is told when a document changes; the plugin's readme lists the cache plugins it tells by itself. If you withdraw a post and it is still being served, this test will say so."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:335
msgid "No cache is holding the blyg"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: a length of time, such as "5 mins"
#: src/Admin/SiteHealth.php:337
#, php-format
msgid "No cache in front of this site keeps the blyg's documents for longer than the cache lifetime in the plugin's settings (%s)."
msgstr ""

